{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Collection Item","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404024","type":"Type"}],"id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/archive/collection/georgia-okeeffe-foundation-photographs","identified_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"accession number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300312355"}],"content":"MS.57","type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"repository number","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404621"}],"content":null,"type":"Identifier"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"preferred term","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300404670"}],"content":"Georgia O'Keeffe Foundation Photographs","type":"Name"}],"produced_by":{"carried_out_by":[],"timespan":{"type":"TimeSpan"},"type":"Production"},"referred_to_by":[{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Related Material","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/relatedmaterial"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003ePart of this collection was accessioned into the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum's art collection under the same accession number, 2006.6.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eGeorgia O'Keeffe Photographs (MS.37 / 2014.3) is located at the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum and contains photographs previously in O'Keeffe's possession of a similar nature as the photography in this collection.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Acquisition information","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/acqinfo"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eThis collection was donated to the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum by The Georgia O'Keeffe Foundation in 2006.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Access restriction statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/accessrestrict"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eThe collection is open to the public for research purposes. Digital assets are available for viewing framed materials.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD arrangement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/arrangement"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eOriginal order unknown. Materials arranged in accession number order.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Biographical Historical statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/bioghist"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eAmerican modernist painter Georgia O'Keeffe cultivated her public image through photography as early as 1918 with a series of photographs by Alfred Steiglitz. Photographers followed O'Keeffe to New Mexico, where she permanently moved after Stieglitz's death. Her likeness appeared in magazines such as Time and Architectural Digest, which featured her Abiquiu home and studio. During this time, O'Keeffe developed her own style of photography, capturing snapshots of her home, beloved Chow Chows, and western landscapes. These photographs passed from O'Keeffe's personal collection to The Georgia O'Keeffe Foundation after her death.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Preferred Citation","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/prefercite"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eGeorgia O'Keeffe Foundation Photographs, 1894-ca. 1992, undated. Georgia O'Keeffe Museum.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Processing Information","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/processinfo"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eThis collection was inventoried by Kelly Swickard. Photographs were arranged loosely into groups based on subject matter by Barbara Buhler Lynes. Elizabeth Ehrnst continued processing. Final processing completed by Ashley Baranyk in 2022.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe majority of this collection is digitized.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"abstract","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/abstract"}],"content":"This collection includes photographic materials related to Georgia O'Keeffe, her properties, travel, and artwork dating from 1894 to circa 1992. In addition to photographic prints and film, there are also original enclosures such as envelopes, boxes, and albums.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Scope and Content statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/scopecontent"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eThis collection contains over 1100 photographs, including copy prints, contact sheets, film, and Polaroids relating to the life and work of Georgia O'Keeffe. The collection includes photography by O'Keeffe that reflects her daily life and photography interests, as well as photography of O'Keeffe and her properties, artwork, and travel. A small portion of the collection relates to The Georgia O'Keeffe Foundation and the catalogue raisonne. Copy prints in the collection are often by fine art photographers such as Alfred Stieglitz, Laura Gilpin, or Eliot Porter and come from other repositories. There are a small number of original enclosures, such as envelopes, boxes, and albums. Part of this collection was accessioned into the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum's art collection under the same accession number, 2006.6, and contains fine art photography by artists like Stieglitz, Todd Webb, and Ansel Adams.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Restrictions on use","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eCopies may be made for research purposes only. For copy prints whose originals and copyright are held by other repositories, copies are not permitted; researchers should contact the repository holding the original regarding copyright.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"\u003cp\u003eGift of The Georgia O'Keeffe Foundation.\u003c/p\u003e","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"EAD Legal status statement","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/userestrict"}],"content":"This collection is the physical property of the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum. The Museum holds rights only for material created by Museum personnel or given to the Museum with such rights specifically assigned. The collection is subject to all copyright laws. The researcher assumes full responsibility for observing all copyright, property, and libel laws as they apply. Contact the Archivist for further copyright and publication information as it pertains to this collection.","type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}